t Minions. [OAL-099]"},{"heading":"Abilities","level":2,"wikitext":"Despite their low stats, Calbolg Titans are strong as they stand together to form an army. They are not known to possess any special powerful magical abilities; however, each carries a barbed spear similar to Gybolg's. {{source|TCG:OAL-099|OAL-099}}","text":"Despite their low stats, Calbolg Titans are strong as they stand together to form an army. They are not known to possess any special powerful magical abilities; however, each carries a barbed spear similar to Gybolg's. [OAL-099]"},{"heading":"Trivia","level":2,"wikitext":"* Calbolg may be named after [[wikipedia:Caladbolg|Caladbolg]], a legendary sword in Gaelic myths that was used several people including Fergus mac Róich.\n[[Category:Gaia-Titans]]\n[[Category:Titans]]\n[[Category:Average Titans]]\n[[Category:Warrior Titans]]\n[[Category:TCG Titans]]\n{{Clear}}{{GaiaBox}}","text":"• Calbolg may be named after Caladbolg, a legendary sword in Gaelic myths that was used several people including Fergus mac Róich."}],"full_text":"Calbolg is a Titan that can be specially summoned by Gybolg to fight alongside him and to form an army.\n\nHistory\n\nCalbolg Titans can be summoned by Gybolg in the same way that Bazela's Hive summons the Bazela's Insect fliers and that Ymir summons the Ice Creatures and Frost Minions. [OAL-099]\n\nAbilities\n\nDespite their low stats, Calbolg Titans are strong as they stand together to form an army. They are not known to possess any special powerful magical abilities; however, each carries a barbed spear similar to Gybolg's. [OAL-099]\n\nTrivia\n\n• Calbolg may be named after Caladbolg, a legendary sword in Gaelic myths that was used several people including Fergus mac Róich.","raw_wikitext":"{{Infobox Titan\n| image   = File:Calbolg.png\n| attack  = 1\n| defense = 1\n| type    = [[Gaia-Titan]] Warrior\n| size    = Average\n| users   = [[Cú Chulainn]]<br>[[Scarlet Byrne]]\n| first   = [[TCG: OAL-009|OAL-009]] (mentioned) <br> [[TCG: OAL-099|OAL-099]]\n}}'''Calbolg''' is a [[Titan]] that can be specially summoned by [[Gybolg]] to fight alongside him and to form an army.\n\n== History ==\nCalbolg Titans can be summoned by Gybolg in the same way that [[Bazela's Hive]] summons the [[Bazela's Insect]] fliers and that [[Ymir]] summons the [[Ice Creature]]s and [[Frost Minion]]s. {{source|TCG:OAL-099|OAL-099}}\n\n== Abilities ==\nDespite their low stats, Calbolg Titans are strong as they stand together to form an army. They are not known to possess any special powerful magical abilities; however, each carries a barbed spear similar to Gybolg's. {{source|TCG:OAL-099|OAL-099}}\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Calbolg may be named after [[wikipedia:Caladbolg|Caladbolg]], a legendary sword in Gaelic myths that was used several people including Fergus mac Róich.\n[[Category:Gaia-Titans]]\n[[Category:Titans]]\n[[Category:Average Titans]]\n[[Category:Warrior Titans]]\n[[Category:TCG Titans]]\n{{Clear}}{{GaiaBox}}","categories":["Average Titans","Gaia-Titans","TCG Titans","Titans","Warrior Titans"],"links":[{"target_id":"huntik:page:2826","status":"resolved","target_title":"Gaia-Titan","label":"Gaia-Titan","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Gaia-Titan","href":"#/categories?name=Gaia-Titans"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:21116","status":"resolved","target_title":"Cú Chulainn","label":"Cú Chulainn","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/C%C3%BA_Chulainn","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A21116"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:3099","status":"resolved","target_title":"Scarlet Byrne","label":"Scarlet Byrne","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Scarlet_Byrne","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A3099"},{"target_title":"TCG: OAL-009","label":"OAL-009","target_id":null,"target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/TCG:_OAL-009","status":"unresolved"},{"target_title":"TCG: OAL-099","label":"OAL-099","target_id":null,"target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/TCG:_OAL-099","status":"unresolved"},{"target_id":"